 "result": "**Mechanism:** a `contextvars.ContextVar` plus werkzeug `LocalProxy` objects.\n\n- `src/tessel/globals.py:40` defines `_app_var: ContextVar[AppContext]`, a single context var that holds the current `AppContext`.\n- `active_app` (`globals.py:44`), `g` (`:47`), `request` (`:57`) and `session` (`:60`) are `LocalProxy(_app_var, \"<attr>\")`. Each lookup reads the current `AppContext` from `_app_var` and takes the attribute `app`, `g`, `request` or `session`. `app_ctx` (`:41`) proxies the context itself.\n- `src/tessel/ctx.py:433` (`AppContext.push`) calls `_app_var.set(self)` and stores the token in `_cv_token`. `ctx.py:498` (`pop`) calls `_app_var.reset(token)`.\n- If nothing is pushed, the proxy raises the \"Working outside of application/request context\" error. `request` and `session` use the request-specific message, and the app context exposes `has_request` for that check (`ctx.py:232`).\n\nBecause a `ContextVar` is isolated per thread and per coroutine, each one resolves to its own object.",
